# Rename to .gitignore in your map repository.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.idea/
.claude/settings.local.json

# draw.io editor backups (.$<name>.drawio.bkp)
.$*.bkp

# Runner artifacts: failure screenshots AND saved browser sessions
# (.runner/state/*.json). Browser state is a credential — it never enters
# version control, even in a private repository.
.runner/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A RUN WRITES — ALL OF IT, NO EXCEPTIONS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Even in a private repository this is worth keeping deliberate. A run output is
# the most sensitive thing here and the least reviewed: nobody reads a 40 MB
# device log before committing it, and git keeps it forever in every clone.
#
# A recorded run is a folder in the runs store (schema/run.yaml); what runs
# learn for the next run is in the state store; a contracted dataset is in the
# datasets store. All three sit beside the lib's tree in a shared data tree or
# inside this one, and none of them is ever committed: the framework's check.py
# fails a results/ or state/ folder under a site or a project. The evidence
# behind a published number is kept by the project's `keep` and cited by its
# run id, not by a commit.
#
# Blanket, and with no negations: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded. Layout docs belong beside the workflow instead.
runs/
state/
datasets/
results/
**/results/
